// emit: ast
// `pub` applies to items with a name and to fields, but not to the entry
// function, which nothing calls (`parser::misplaced-pub`); before anything
// else, such as a variant, a parameter, a `let` or another `pub`, it is
// `parser::unexpected-token` (ADR 0050). A `mod` inside a function is
// `parser::local-mod` (ADR 0049). In a path, `super` follows only `super`
// at the start, and `crate` comes only first. After an error in the last
// item of a module, parsing resumes at the module's `}`, which closes it:
// no `parser::unclosed-block` is reported, and the items after it are not
// in it (tested in `src/syntax/parser.rs`, since this dump shows errors).
